  "query_preview": "..\nA slight increase in moisture associated with a surface trough will \nbring scattered showers to Tinian and Saipan after midnight, becoming\nisolated in the early afternoon. On the other hand, Rota and Guam \nwill remain in an isolated shower regime through midweek. Starting \nlate tomorrow morning, the western coastal waters of Guam may see \nprominent cloud and shower buildup due to island heating moving \noffshore. Model guidance indicates limited vertical moisture and a \nlack of upper- level support compared to what we've seen in the \nprevious days. However, if the island- effect showers can overcome \nthese limitations, Guam's western coastal waters should not rule out \na thunderstorm or two. Invest 92W (see Tropical Systems section \nbelow) is continuing its WNW trek towards the Marianas. Confidence is\nstill low as models show a wide spread in timing and intensity as it\napproaches the region. Regardless of its stage in development, the \nMarianas should prepare for wetter weather in the latter half of the \nweek, possibly clearing up over the weekend. We will continue to \nmonitor Invest 92W and communicate any significant updates.",
